  "body": "Stacked on #1137 (on #1045, #1005). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nThread milling (internal and external) gains pass control, one value `ThreadPasses` on the kernel's `ThreadParams` and on `OpParams::Thread`:\n\n- **Decreasing pass depths (constant chip area)**: `pass_schedule: constant_area` - cumulative depth after pass i of n is `D x sqrt(i/n)`, the infeed is the first (largest) pass, `n = ceil((D/infeed)^2)`, capped at 64 (refused by name past that). The last roughing pass lands exactly on D.\n- **Finishing pass** of its own radial depth (`finish_depth`) and **spring passes** (`spring_passes`, at most 4) on the final radius.\n- **Depth allowance** (`depth_allowance`, radial): the last pass lands on standard depth - allowance. A negative allowance (past the major diameter of a hole / the design root of a boss) and one over a quarter of the thread depth are refused by name.\n- **Spindle and cutter hand** (`spindle_reverse` = M4, `cutter_left_hand`): climb sense flips under M4 (the helix keeps the drawing's hand); a right-hand-cut mill under M4 or a left-hand-cut one under M3 is refused by name. M4 reaches the post via a new `PARAM MillSpindle reverse` (`post::ask_reverse_spindle`) and manifest flag `millSpindleReverse`; `fanuc.cps` declares it and writes `M4`; the engine refuses such a section by name for every other script (the lathe's #629 `SpindleDirection`/`threadHands` is deliberately not reused).\n- Gated at the door (create, edit, retool via `thread_op::door`) and again in the kernel. File/MCP keys flattened into the Thread params, additive, written only when not default; the digest clause appears only when not default. Page: Passes tab (schedule, finish, spring, allowance), Feeds tab (spindle, cutter hand).\n\nDefaults are the #894 ride: every existing thread golden (`.cl` and `.nc`) is byte-identical.\n\n## Sources\n\nSmid, \"CNC Programming Handbook\" (thread cutting: constant-area pass depths, spring pass); Machinery's Handbook (\"Thread milling\", \"Thread cutting\": finish pass, climb vs cutter rotation, cutter hand vs spindle); ISO 724 / ISO 965-1 (depths, tolerance scale). No HSMWorks / Fusion material. Decisions in `docs/decisions/988-thread-pass-control.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Kernel (`camcraft-motion`, `machining2d::thread_pass_tests`): `constant_area_passes_decrease_and_each_takes_the_same_chip_area`, `a_finishing_pass_and_spring_passes_land_on_the_final_radius`, `an_allowance_leaves_the_stated_depth_uncut_and_is_refused_past_its_tolerance`, `an_m4_spindle_with_a_left_hand_cut_mill_flips_the_orbit_and_keeps_the_hand`, `a_cutter_hand_against_the_spindle_and_other_nonsense_are_refused_by_name`.\n- App (`tests/thread_passes.rs`): clean verify + Fanuc post for decreasing/finish/spring/allowance; M4 left-hand ride posts `M4` on Fanuc and is refused by name on Haas; door refusals at creation; edit gated, undo, project-file round trip.\n- Golden: `thread_mill_constant_area_spring_pass.cl` (`golden_cl::thread_mill_constant_area_spring_pass_matches_golden`).\n- MCP: `mcp::thread_pass_control_over_the_params_door`.\n- UI: `thread_mill_page_tests::the_pass_control_rows_edit_the_draft_and_apply_undoes`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/985-external-threads`: green on the final head (post, motion, app, ui suites; 13.5 min); clippy -D warnings on motion/app/post/ui.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- M4 on posts other than Fanuc (they refuse by name). No machine run.\n- The issue's last bullet (feed starts at the op's `top_z` R plane rather than each hole's entry) is split out to #1212.\n\nChangelog: Thread milling: decreasing (constant chip area) pass depths, a finishing pass, spring passes, a depth allowance and M4 / left-hand-cut thread mills, internal and external (#988)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #988\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
